## The fixed tests

1. tests/storytime-cover-guards.test.ts, test CVG9. The form chosen: a read-only check of the
   scan path. The test reads the real cover cost file with parseCostsTsv and keeps the rows at or
   after the cover start time. It compares the count and the spend of those rows with the rows of
   scanCoverCostFiles of the unit root of the repository, and the guard decision of the real cover
   spec gives the run cover and the same spend. The second part of the test uses a unit root
   outside the repository. That root holds a fixture row with its own row id, and the production
   path never sees that row. The test creates, writes, changes, and deletes nothing under the
   real out/ folder.
2. tests/storytime-u2-guards.test.ts, tests U2G11 and U2G10. The form chosen: a temp ROOT. The
   test copies scripts/storytime-muse.mjs and scripts/storytime-muse-guards.mjs into a temp
   repository, links the node_modules folder, and runs the CLI there with a temp HOME. The CLI
   and the guard resolve their root from the path of the script, so every write of the CLI stays
   in the temp folder. The test deletes only temp folders. The two deletes of the real unit 2
   folder and the real family-word folder are gone. This file is not in the owned paths of the
   specification. The change stays in the harness of the 2 tests.

